🏁 Tips for Best Results

Use a real USB shifter and pedals
If you have a USB manual shifter + clutch pedals, games like BeamNG.drive become much more effective at teaching coordination between clutch and stick — far better than keyboard alone.

Combine gaming with real-world practice
Simulators can help you understand gear timing, clutch coordination, stalling, and rev matching, but they cannot fully replicate the physical feel of the clutch bite point. It’s best to combine simulator practice with real lessons or time in a real manual car.

